    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to students’ pace and style. For example, they can generate practice problems tailored to individual weaknesses, provide instant feedback, and explain concepts in simple terms. This helps build confidence and makes math more engaging without overwhelming students."
